# Proof

## Givens (Evidence)
- evidence_6: Users authenticate once and expect to stay signed in for 14–30 days on trusted devices.
- evidence_7: Industry-standard session timeouts span 15 minutes (banking) to 30 days (social).
- evidence_8: SOC2 audit requires session revocation within 60 seconds of a credential-compromise event.

## Lemmas (Propositions)
- proposition_9: Session timeout must be configurable per-deployment in the range [15min, 30days].
- proposition_10: Sessions must be revocable server-side within 60 seconds.

## Theorems (Resolutions)
- resolution_15: Store the session token in an httpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax cookie; never expose to JavaScript.
- resolution_16: Regenerate the session id immediately after successful authentication and after any privilege change.

--- end render preview ---
